# ============================================================================
# Stock Watch — environment configuration
# ============================================================================
# COPY THIS FILE TO ".env" (drop the .example) AND PUT YOUR REAL KEYS IN IT.
#
#   .env is git-ignored, so your keys never get committed.
#   This .env.example file is safe to commit — it contains no real values.
#
# Rules that will save you pain:
#   - Do NOT wrap values in quotes
#   - Do NOT put spaces around the "="
#   - Do NOT leave a trailing space after the value
# ============================================================================

# --- Benzinga (licensed market data) ----------------------------------------
# Powers: bull/bear cases, earnings, wire news, options flow, economic calendar.
# Get one at https://www.benzinga.com/apis  ·  manage at https://www.api.benzinga.com/token
BENZINGA_API_KEY=bz.your_key_here

# --- Anthropic (AI analysis button) -----------------------------------------
# Get one at https://console.anthropic.com -> API keys. Billable per call.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your_key_here

# Optional: override the model. Defaults to claude-sonnet-5.
# AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# --- Display ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Timezone used for "today", the Key Dates tab, and all displayed times.
APP_TIMEZONE=America/Chicago

# --- Optional tuning --------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=3000
# MAX_EARNINGS_TICKERS=600     # cap on tickers priced per earnings load
# EARNINGS_MAX_PAGES=15        # Yahoo calendar pagination attempts

# --- Corporate proxy (only if you need one) ---------------------------------
# Node ignores the Windows system proxy, so set it explicitly if your network
# requires one. Leave commented out otherwise — and never set this on Render.
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://your-proxy-host:port

# --- Coupons (optional) -----------------------------------------------------
# Rakuten does NOT give you a permanent API key. You get a Client ID + Client
# Secret from the Developer Portal (Account > Applications), and a SID from
# the top right of your Publisher Dashboard. The app swaps those three for a
# short-lived token automatically and refreshes it — set once, forget.
#
#   Developer Portal:  https://developers.rakutenadvertising.com/
#   SID (Scope ID):    top right of the Rakuten Advertising publisher dashboard
#
# The Client Secret is a password. Never commit it, never paste it in chat.
# COUPON_PROVIDER=rakuten
# COUPON_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id
# COUPON_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret
# COUPON_SCOPE_ID=your_sid
#
# Alternative: a pre-minted bearer token, used as-is. It WILL expire and the
# app cannot refresh it, so prefer the three values above.
# COUPON_API_TOKEN=your_affiliate_network_token
